# `q.toLowerCase()` answers the same in every iteration, but a `break` comes before it: hoisted, a loop that leaves in its first iteration would pay for a call that the program does not make.
# The header of the specialized version has a parameter for the result, which is absent at first. The iteration that finds it absent makes the call; the others take what came round.
# RUN: walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK: string|absent @JSValue) isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true:
# CHECK: testedType=absent
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch
# CHECK-NEXT: frequency=Unlikely isInLoop=true:
# CHECK: inlineBuiltin=StringToLowerCase
# CHECK-NEXT: Jump -> next
# CHECK: = Narrowed
# CHECK-NEXT: Jump -> next
# CHECK-NOT: inlineBuiltin=StringToLowerCase
# -- source: lazy-call-after-break.ts
